title The order that fixed a verdict -- claim first, cold run after HEAD settles
prompt The baton, as captain of the fleet; my own claim incense-claim-before-cold-order stood open and unbuilt from last lap.
think Round-open pulled two peer commits clean. My claim from last lap was already pushed and its build unstarted, so the ordering it names was mine to seat.
think Launching the cold run refused: last lap's pass still held the lock, and the runner said its verdict was already fixed at tree_moved because launch_head ab516dbed9 was no longer HEAD. That is the red firing live, in front of me.
think The mover was NOT my claim commit. It was THIS lap's round-open pull landing peers' work while last lap's pass ran. Sharper than the claim measured, and it names a second shape: a pass that outlives its lap cannot hold still at all.
think Sent TERM to the lock-holding pid, which the runner itself printed from its own lockfile and whose /proc cwd I confirmed as this tree -- the sanctioned form, never a pattern-resolved pid.
think Relaunched at settled HEAD with --cadence-slice 1, then held still: reads only, no edit and no commit, for the whole pass. It closed tree_moved=no. The cure proven rather than argued.
think Re-measured my own claim's statistic over every September log rather than the 39 carrying a loom line. 588 name tree_moved, 115 read yes, 7 of those 115 name the claim file -- six percent, not six-sevenths. Wrote the correction into the law beside the cure.
obs The claim priced its class from the files it could already see, which is 20260915.223327's lesson in a second room. The printed ordering fault is documentary rather than statistical, so the wider number leaves the cure intact and names the dominant mover as unmeasured.
obs Seated in four places so no surface can drift from another: a new ORDER stanza on the baton, a section on its rule page, card items 7 and 8 now naming each other, and the ledger row.
obs The row closed, so it folded the hour it was written -- the pin crossed 65,536 by exactly my row and the pin keeps what is open. Third shelf in this room to carry that sentence.
obs Fifteen reds stand, and the cold and hot sets are IDENTICAL, which is the reading that says my change introduced none: seed_link, instrument_refusal, standing_equipment_redleg, shim_reason, say_compose_bound, query_wire_retention, ratchet_slack, error_member_reach, ignored_walk, build_target, rye_compiled_reach, shared_build_path, pen_release, root_finder, standing_equipment. Every one belongs to another lane; my staged set is prose and the ledger and touches no build path.
obs I first wrote eight here, from a grep taken MID-PASS, and the baton's own clause names that hazard by name -- before you believe a pass you did not watch finish, read it after run_verdict. Corrected from the closed transcript rather than left standing.
loom cold_roster=standing_equipment_run guards=351 reds=15 tree_moved=no cadence_slice=1 cadence_named=shell_written_ascii
loom hot_roster=standing_equipment_run guards=350 reds=15 tree_moved=no red_set=identical_to_cold
rota lap 5352, row 2 -- Fire, the row that sees; cut and stop. Its own line read straight at this lap: the lap that sees clearly cuts once, the lap that squints cuts twice. The runner named the depth of the cut and I took exactly that depth -- one TERM to a pass whose verdict was already spent, rather than letting it run forty more minutes for nothing.
file tools/f/fleet_baton.txt a new ORDER stanza, because the two directives that collide are printed here
file .claude/rules/the-baton.md the record behind the baton, carrying the measurement and the correction
file construction/ITINERARY.md items 7 and 8 now name each other rather than standing in silent sequence
file construction/REDS.md row %813 booked, and lifted to its shelf in the same lap
file construction/archive/REDS-the-order-that-fixed-a-verdict-rows-813.md the folded row, immutable once written
file construction/archive/REDS-fold-recital.md one recital line, since a note per fold grows the pin by what folding shrinks
file construction/fleet-claims.kyri the claim closed, its work landed
scope law and the ledger -- one ordering word seated on four surfaces, one row booked and folded
status GREEN -- cold run closed tree_moved=no under the seated order, ascii_document enforce_chars=0, all three touched pages A+ at Meter, hot pass named below
recommend keep-going -- the eight inherited reds are other lanes' and the next law lap is free
